<%--
Attachment_Thumbnail

THE way a thumbnail renders in an RSX app - images, PDFs, Office documents, everything. A caller
supplies an attachment id and a size; the component fetches the record, builds the URL, and keeps
the picture correct for as long as it is on screen.

It matters that this is a component and not a URL string in a payload: an Office document has no
thumbnail until the background render worker has produced its PDF rendition, so what the browser
first paints is an extension-icon placeholder. When the render lands, a realtime frame on the
attachment brings the component back for a fresh record and the picture swaps in place - no reload,
no polling, and no stale placeholder pinned by a one-year cache header. An attachment pointed at
other bytes (relink_storage()) swaps the same way: the URL carries the record's content version,
so the refetched record yields another URL.

Args:
  $attachment_id  (required) - the File_Attachment_Model id. Throws if absent.
  $type           (optional) - dynamic variant: 'fit' (default) or 'cover'.
  $width          (optional) - dynamic variant width in px (default 120).
  $height         (optional) - dynamic variant height in px; omitted -> width-only variant.
  $preset         (optional) - named preset from rsx.thumbnails.presets. MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE with
                               $type/$width/$height - passing both throws.
  $alt            (optional) - img alt text; defaults to the attachment's file name.
  $allow_animated (optional) - true: an ANIMATED image (a GIF, an animated WebP or PNG - the
                               attachment's is_animated) is shown as the ORIGINAL file, playing,
                               in place of its still first-frame thumbnail. Default false. Every
                               other attachment is unaffected. The original is the full upload,
                               which may be megabytes where a thumbnail is kilobytes, so it is for
                               a single picture a page presents, not a grid of them. Its box: a
                               dynamic variant's $width / $height are applied to the image
                               ('cover' crops to them, 'fit' fits inside them); with $preset the
                               image is bounded by the host's own CSS (max-width: 100%).

Extra classes go on the invocation as an ordinary HTML attribute - <Attachment_Thumbnail class="me-2"
$attachment_id=id /> - which jqhtml preserves on the host element; there is no $class arg.

States (data-render-status, on the rendered <img> or placeholder, carries the blob's
File_Storage_Model::RENDER_STATUS_*, or 'none' when there is no resident blob):
  1 NOT_REQUIRED - an image or PDF: the picture is rasterized straight from the blob.
  2 PENDING      - queued for render: the extension icon is served, uncacheable.
  3 RENDERED     - the real page-1 raster.
  4 FAILED       - the last render attempt failed: the extension icon, uncacheable.
  unavailable    - the record could not be fetched (deleted, or not visible to this user).

Events OUT:
  'preview_loaded' {attachment_id, state, render_status, variant, natural_width, natural_height}
    What this component put on screen. ALWAYS eventually emitted, whatever that was: a host
    listens for it and never reaches for the <img>. Emitted once the <img> has settled (at once
    for a picture the browser already holds) and again after every change of what is shown - the
    realtime swap, a reload() after $attachment_id changed. A subscriber that registers late is
    handed the last report; one that registers while the next picture is loading waits for it.
    (NOT 'loaded' - that is a reserved jqhtml lifecycle event fired internally with no data.)

      state           'loaded'       the picture has decoded: the raster, or the type icon of a
                                     file that has no raster.
                      'preparing'    the extension icon of a PENDING render has decoded; the
                                     swap follows and reports again.
                      'failed'       the image could not be loaded or decoded, or it is the
                                     extension icon of a FAILED render.
                      'unavailable'  the empty box of a record that could not be fetched.
      render_status   the data-render-status value above (the id, 'none' or 'unavailable').
      variant         'thumbnail' (a generated thumbnail or extension icon was requested),
                      'original' ($allow_animated showed the upload itself), null with no image.
      natural_width,  of the image actually served - the upload's own size only under
      natural_height  'original'. 0 when no image decoded.
--%>
<Define:Attachment_Thumbnail tag="div">
    <% if (!this.args.attachment_id) { throw new Error('Attachment_Thumbnail requires $attachment_id'); } %>
    <% if (this.args.preset && (this.args.type || this.args.width || this.args.height)) { throw new Error('Attachment_Thumbnail: $preset and $type/$width/$height are mutually exclusive'); } %>
    <%
        const _record = this.data.attachment;
        const _status = (_record && _record.file_storage) ? int(_record.file_storage.render_status_id) : 'none';
        const _alt = this.args.alt || (_record ? _record.file_name : '');
        const _src = _record ? File_Attachment_Model.thumbnail_url(_record, {
            type: this.args.type,
            width: this.args.width || 120,
            height: this.args.height,
            preset: this.args.preset,
        }) : null;
    %>
    <%
        // The original, playing, in place of the still: only when the caller asked and the
        // image really is animated.
        const _animated = this.args.allow_animated === true && !!_record && !!_record.is_animated;
        const _fit = this.args.type === 'cover' ? 'cover' : 'fit';
    %>
    <% if (_animated && this.args.preset) { %>
        <img class="Attachment_Thumbnail__img Attachment_Thumbnail__img--animated" src="<%= File_Attachment_Model.inline_url(_record) %>" alt="<%= _alt %>" data-render-status="<%= _status %>" data-attachment-id="<%= int(this.args.attachment_id) %>">
    <% } else if (_animated && this.args.height) { %>
        <img class="Attachment_Thumbnail__img Attachment_Thumbnail__img--animated Attachment_Thumbnail__img--<%= _fit %>" src="<%= File_Attachment_Model.inline_url(_record) %>" width="<%= int(this.args.width || 120) %>" height="<%= int(this.args.height) %>" alt="<%= _alt %>" data-render-status="<%= _status %>" data-attachment-id="<%= int(this.args.attachment_id) %>">
    <% } else if (_animated) { %>
        <img class="Attachment_Thumbnail__img Attachment_Thumbnail__img--animated" src="<%= File_Attachment_Model.inline_url(_record) %>" width="<%= int(this.args.width || 120) %>" alt="<%= _alt %>" data-render-status="<%= _status %>" data-attachment-id="<%= int(this.args.attachment_id) %>">
    <% } else if (_src) { %>
        <img class="Attachment_Thumbnail__img" src="<%= _src %>" alt="<%= _alt %>" data-render-status="<%= _status %>" data-attachment-id="<%= int(this.args.attachment_id) %>">
    <% } else { %>
        <%-- No record: deleted, or not visible to this user. A quiet empty box, never an error. --%>
        <div class="Attachment_Thumbnail__placeholder" data-render-status="unavailable" data-attachment-id="<%= int(this.args.attachment_id) %>"></div>
    <% } %>
</Define:Attachment_Thumbnail>
